# ripgrep config, symlinked to ~/.ripgreprc and loaded via the
# RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH export in ~/.clirc (rg has no color env var, so a
# config file is the only way to theme it).
#
# Format: one argument per line, no shell quoting, no inline comments —
# a `#` only starts a comment at the beginning of a line.
#
# Colors are ANSI palette indices matching the shell prompt, so they follow
# the terminal theme. See the palette table in cli/.clirc before editing:
#   11 bright yellow = paths (same as the prompt's dir segment)
#   14 bright cyan   = line/column numbers (same as the prompt's λ)
#    9 bright red    = the match itself (same as the prompt's username)

--colors=path:fg:11
--colors=path:style:bold
--colors=line:fg:14
--colors=column:fg:14
--colors=match:fg:9
--colors=match:style:bold
